!-----------------------------------------------------------------------
!
! Absorption cross-section CH3Cl: CH3Cl + hv --> products
! source : JPL-2006 (no change with respect to JPL-2002)
! http://www.atmosphere.mpg.de/enid/2295
! -> Catalogue -> "Halogeno-alkanes, -alkyl radicals" -> "C+H+Cl" -> "CH3Cl" -> "JPL-2002"
! Rem1: Quantum yield = 1 (no explicit information).
! Rem2: Temperature influence:
!   i) 174-216nm: T dep. according to the formula:
!           log10 crs = sum An*wl^n + (T-273)*sum Bn*wl^n
!       where An and Bn are parameters introduced in CRS_CFC.
!       The cross sections are computed in subroutine CRS_TDEP.
!   ii) JPL-2006 (=JPL-2002) provides crs for wl > 216nm without mentioning
!       whether there are only available for T=295-298K. Assuming this is the case,
!       I did not take them.
!-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Begins at wl interval :        46  | Finishes at wl interval :   66
!-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
!  no  from(nm) to(nm)  | crs (cm2) | qyield (0->1) |   Tdep_param1 |   Tdep_param2
!-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
